  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Kamakhya Temple, located in Guwahati on the banks of the Brahmaputra River, is one of the most significant Shakti Pitha temples in India. Dedicated to Goddess Kamakhya (a form of Durga), the temple is believed to be one of the 51 Shakti Pithas—sacred sites associated with Hindu goddess worship. The temple's distinctive hilltop location and ancient origins make it a major pilgrimage destination.\n\nThe temple complex houses sanctums dedicated to different manifestations of the goddess, including Kali, Tara, and other forms. The unique Assamese architectural style, with its beehive-shaped dome, reflects the region's cultural heritage. The temple attracts millions of devotees annually, particularly during Navratri and Ambubachi Mela festivals, making it one of Assam's most important religious centers.",
